{"abstract":"This paper explores a theoretical framework called “recollecting” for Participatory Design (PD) with collectives to support coexistence in times of uncertainty and polarisation around climate crises. It offers a PD concept and design approach that engages with the memories of hybrid collectives of humans and more-than-human actors within transitions of their built and natural environment, foregrounding collective memory as a political and relational process, central to shaping regenerative futures. In contrast to dominant strategies for dealing with climate challenges that emphasise technical solutions and material flows, we argue that meaningful transitions require practices of remembering - ritualised, situated, and affective - embedded in local ecologies and histories. We examine three case studies across Belgium, Denmark, and Sweden where PD researchers collaborated with local governments and communities to reimagine relations among people, places, and more-than-human actors. Through these cases, we identify three interwoven dimensions of recollecting: “orienting” towards attachments and past relations, “actualising” memory to shift power dynamics, and “archiving” as co-creating dynamic repositories of collective memory that enable continuity, reflection and action across time and actors. Our findings suggest that recollecting can support transitions not only by regenerating ecosystems, but also by reshuffling social and ecological inequalities. Ultimately, we argue that designing with collectives offers pathways toward addressing regenerative futures grounded in recognition, care and solidarity.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Huybrechts, Liesbeth","Tsenova, Violeta","Jönsson, Li","den Eynde, Dolores Van","Wehlitz, Anna-Mamusu","Binder, Thomas","Fritsch, Jonas","Palmieri, Teresa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-884852"],"filters":{"added":"2026-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Belgium","Italy","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hasselt University","Libera Università di Bolzano","Malmö University"],"keyword":["Collectives","Participatory design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"recollecting with collectives towards coexistence a theoretical framework for participatory design in times of climate crises","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3796624.3796642","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-884852","ids":["itu-cc90422c-9239-420d-83b5-76113a7d3eee"],"keyword":["Collectives","Participatory design","Recollecting"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-82EAA806EAC91291B6194F732B260CE5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3796624.3796642","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["The Department, People and Computational Things"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"be","key":"hasselt university","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Hasselt University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"malmö university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Malmö University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"it","key":"libera università di bolzano","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Libera Università di Bolzano","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Liesbeth","key":"huybrechtspau","last":"Huybrechts","name":"Huybrechts, Liesbeth","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Violeta","key":"tsenovapau","last":"Tsenova","name":"Tsenova, Violeta","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Li","key":"jönssonpau","last":"Jönsson","name":"Jönsson, Li","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Dolores Van","key":"deneyndepau","last":"den Eynde","name":"den Eynde, Dolores Van","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna-Mamusu Sesay","key":"wehlitzpau","last":"Wehlitz","locid":"dda395cd-41ec-469e-a3e9-b1c024bbb1a7","name":"Wehlitz, Anna-Mamusu","name_org":"Wehlitz, Anna-Mamusu Sesay","orcid":"0000-0002-0647-6101","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"binderpau","last":"Binder","locid":"c90e23c6-5bf4-4d6f-97d8-b162b8a5b03e","name":"Binder, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0001-8244-1798","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpau","last":"Fritsch","locid":"d37cba38-dff2-4c27-a515-226cfadfd849","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0001-9065-2843","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Teresa","key":"palmieripau","last":"Palmieri","name":"Palmieri, Teresa","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3796624.3796642","eisbn":["9798400721052"],"issn":["21505896"],"pages":"363-373","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","series":"Proceedings of the Participatory Design Conference","status":"p","title":"PDC '26: Proceedings of the 19th Participatory Design Conference 2026, Vol. 1: Full Papers","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-cc90422c-9239-420d-83b5-76113a7d3eee"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Recollecting with Collectives towards Coexistence: A Theoretical Framework for Participatory Design in Times of Climate Crises","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-884852","year":"2026","yearsub":"2026"}
{"abstract":"This paper explores speculation otherwise by tracing how speculative potential emerges from the very 5rst encounters of design research. Rather than viewing speculation as a designer-led projection of possible futures, we propose a shift toward understanding speculation as something to be recognized within already unfolding worlds. Drawing on Tsing’s notion of contamination and Ingold’s concept of correspondence, we show how design engagements evolve through entanglements with speculartive forces circulating in the everyday: through material residues, infrastructural rhythms, social negotiations, and more-than-human relations. Through slow alignments, tentative invitations, failed funding applications and walks through neighbourhood sites, we describe how our own imaginaries became entangled with worlds of urban transformation. We argue that what is often framed as a pre-project phase is already a site of speculative formation. Speculation otherwise thus positions design as attuned participation in unfolding situations, engaging not by projecting futures, but by corresponding with speculative possibilities already in motion.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Wehlitz, Anna-Mamusu","Binder, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-884855"],"filters":{"added":"2026-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Contamination","Correspondence","design engagements"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"toward speculation otherwise correspondence and contamination in design engagements with urban renewal","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21606/drs.2026.2040","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-884855","ids":["itu-d7fb1f32-f333-41f0-86d7-c20fd2ed7116"],"keyword":["contamination;","correspondence","design engagements","speculation otherwise"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9A02390A3C0604A088162C60FC25EEC6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21606/drs.2026.2040","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://dl.designresearchsociety.org/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=4057&context=drs-conference-papers","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna-Mamusu","key":"wehlitzpau","last":"Wehlitz","locid":"dda395cd-41ec-469e-a3e9-b1c024bbb1a7","name":"Wehlitz, Anna-Mamusu","orcid":"0000-0002-0647-6101","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"binderpau","last":"Binder","locid":"c90e23c6-5bf4-4d6f-97d8-b162b8a5b03e","name":"Binder, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0001-8244-1798","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.21606/drs.2026.2040","series":"DRS Biennial Conference Series","status":"p","title":"Design Research Society Conference 2026"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d7fb1f32-f333-41f0-86d7-c20fd2ed7116"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Toward speculation otherwise : Correspondence and contamination in design engagements with urban renewal","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-884855","year":"2026","yearsub":"2026"}
{"abstract":"Blue denim, a billion-dollar industry, is currently dyed with indigo in an unsustainable process requiring harsh reducing and alkaline chemicals. Forming indigo directly in the yarn through indican (indoxyl-β-glucoside) is a promising alternative route with mild conditions. Indican eliminates the requirement for reducing agent while still ending as indigo, the only known molecule yielding the unique hue of blue denim. However, a bulk source of indican is missing. Here, we employ enzyme and process engineering guided by techno-economic analyses to develop an economically viable drop-in indican synthesis technology. Rational engineering of PtUGT1, a glycosyltransferase from the indigo plant, alleviated the severe substrate inactivation observed with the wildtype enzyme at the titers needed for bulk production. We further describe a mild, light-driven dyeing process. Finally, we conduct techno-economic, social sustainability, and comparative life-cycle assessments. These indicate that the presented technologies have the potential to significantly reduce environmental impacts from blue denim dyeing with only a modest cost increase.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Bidart, Gonzalo Nahuel","Teze, David","Jansen, Charlotte Uldahl","Pasutto, Eleonora","Putkaradze, Natalia","Sesay, Anna Mamusu","Fredslund, Folmer","Lo Leggio, Leila","Ögmundarson, Olafur","Sukumara, Sumesh","Qvortrup, Katrine","Welner, Ditte Hededam"],"cuid":["S03-098.38-768467"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Qvortrup, Katrine","Welner, Ditte Hededam"],"country":["Iceland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Iceland"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-U"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-DSKD"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-DSKD","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"chemoenzymatic indican for light driven denim dyeing","src":["dtu","itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-024-45749-3","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-098.38-768467","identifier":[{"id":"38413572","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10899603","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85186235473","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-d78213e6-946e-4833-8da4-f92058de5022","itu-b77d23f7-f586-4239-9e14-7b953762f1b1","ku-c521cd54-bc84-4752-9c43-e087b3e57b84"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-65DE93AB6C733A363D041F47E6C1D142"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/354575581/s41467-024-45749-3.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/385221501/s41467_024_45749_3.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-024-45749-3","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2024","yearSub":"2024"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar"